INT. SYNERGY LOGISTICS - OPEN-PLAN OFFICE - MORNING

Rows of identical desks under beige light. A motivational poster: "TEAMWORK: BECAUSE BLAME IS BETTER SHARED." A fern in the corner, plastic.

TRENT OKAFOR-BUCHANAN (40s, regional director, a lanyard, a mug that says WORLD'S OKAYEST BOSS) stands at a whiteboard. DELPHINE ACHEBE-MARCH (30s, analyst, cardigan, hair in a clip) sits with a laptop. WALTER "WALLY" PRZYBYLSKI-ODUYA (50s, procurement, bifocals, a stress ball) lounges back with his feet up.

TRENT
Okay, so the quarterly numbers.

DELPHINE
They're down.

WALLY
They're soft.

TRENT
They're down but they're soft.

DELPHINE
They're down by thirty-one percent.

WALLY
Which is soft.

TRENT
Delphine, what does the model say?

DELPHINE
The model says we lost the Henderson account.

WALLY
Which wasn't ours.

DELPHINE
It was ours in March.

WALLY
In March everything was ours.

TRENT
Okay. So, whose fault is it?

DELPHINE
It's no one's--

WALLY
Procurement was clean.

DELPHINE
--no one's fault, Trent, it's the market--

TRENT
It has to be someone's fault.

WALLY
It's Delphine's.

DELPHINE
Excuse me?

WALLY
She flagged it late.

DELPHINE
I flagged it in February!

WALLY
After the horse left the barn.

DELPHINE
There was no barn!

TRENT
Guys! Guys.

He holds up a marker. They go still. Trent turns to the whiteboard and writes, with great seriousness, the word: LEARNINGS.

TRENT (CONT'D)
Let's circle back.

WALLY
(muttering)
I hate circling back.

TRENT
What was that?

WALLY
I love it.

Delphine closes her laptop with a loud snap and stands.

DELPHINE
I'm going to get coffee.

TRENT
We're in a meeting.

DELPHINE
It's a stand-up. I'm standing.

She exits. Wally and Trent stare at the empty chair. The fern's plastic leaves tremble in her wake.

WALLY
She's gonna blame me for that.

TRENT
Who?

WALLY
Her. Or him. Or someone.

TRENT
You think she's going to blame you for her leaving?

WALLY
She will. It's her fault, really.

TRENT
Then who's going to take the minutes?

WALLY
Not me.

TRENT
Not me.

They look at the whiteboard. LEARNINGS. Underneath, nothing.
